---
import AppleMark from './AppleMark.astro';
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer class="foot">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="foot__grid">
      <div class="foot__brand">
        <a href="/" class="brand" aria-label="Apple — home">
          <AppleMark size={26} alive={false} />
          <span class="brand__word">Apple</span>
        </a>
        <p class="foot__tag">It works inside the place you already have open.</p>
        {/* THE RENAME LEFT A STUTTER HERE, ON EVERY PAGE. This is the operator's byline and it read
            "Golem Labs". The rebrand rewrote "Golem" to "Apple" wherever it appeared, and this one
            became a bare second "Apple" sitting directly under the "Apple" wordmark in a different
            face, saying nothing the two lines around it do not. Every footer on the site read:
            Apple / one sentence / APPLE.

            The name is not invented to repair it. /terms already publishes the operator — "the AI
            building service for Roblox operated by Apple Labs" — so the byline is restored to the
            name the site itself gives, and /privacy, which had been flattened into "Apple is built
            and operated by Apple", now gives the same one. tests/one-operator.test.mjs holds the
            three in agreement. */}
        <p class="mono">Apple Labs</p>
      </div>

      <nav aria-label="Product" class="foot__col">
        <h2>Product</h2>
        <ul>
          {/* The landing is one viewport; these sections no longer exist as
              anchors. Point at the routes that actually explain them. */}
          <li><a href="/docs/getting-started">How it works</a></li>
          {/* /proof is the one page on this site that shows the product doing something rather than
              describing it — a whole run's log, the counts before and after it, what the game
              reported when it was played, and the five defects the exercise found. It is listed
              under Product and not under Docs because it is not instructions. */}
          <li><a href="/proof">Proof</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/modes">Modes</a></li>
          <li><a href="/changelog">Changelog</a></li>
          <li><a href="/pricing">Pricing</a></li>
          {/* One entry, not two. "Changelog" was listed twice here — the second was a paste, and a
              duplicated nav item reads as a broken page. */}
          <li><a href="/status">Status &amp; known issues</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <nav aria-label="Documentation" class="foot__col">
        <h2>Docs</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/docs/getting-started">Getting started</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/plugin">Studio plugin</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/modes">Modes</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/credits-and-limits">Credits &amp; limits</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/faq">FAQ</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <nav aria-label="Legal and contact" class="foot__col">
        <h2>Legal</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a></li>
          <li><a href="/terms">Terms</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/privacy-and-data">Your data</a></li>
          <li><a href="mailto:apple.labs.app@gmail.com">Contact</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>

    <div class="foot__base">
      {/* THE NON-BREAKING SPACE IS LOAD-BEARING, on a phone, on nineteen pages.

          At 375px on the runner's Linux font metrics this line wrapped so that "as-is." sat alone
          on the last line, on every page this footer appears on, and
          apps/site/tests/rendered-typography.test.mjs failed with "19 text blocks end on a
          stranded word, and the budget is 0". `p { text-wrap: pretty }` in global.css did not
          save it: the engine kept the break.

          Binding the last two words is METRIC-INDEPENDENT. There is no viewport and no font on
          which "as-is." can be stranded any more, because it can no longer be a line by itself —
          which is a stronger fix than tuning a width, and it is why this is in the markup rather
          than in the stylesheet.

          MEASURED both ways in Chromium over the built site, not reasoned about:
            before   360px  ["(c) 2026 Apple. Apple is a beta service, provided", "as-is."]
            after    360px  ["(c) 2026 Apple. Apple is a beta service,", "provided as-is."]
          macOS strands it at 360px and the runner at 375px, which is why the runner's failure did
          not reproduce here at the width the runner named. Anyone re-checking this should sweep
          widths rather than trusting one. */}
      <p>&copy; {year} Apple. Apple is a beta service, provided&nbsp;as-is.</p>
      <p class="foot__disclaimer">
        Not affiliated with or endorsed by Roblox Corporation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  .foot {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) 0 2.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .foot__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(240px, 1.65fr) repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .brand {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .brand:hover {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .brand__word {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  /* The operator's byline, in the body face. It was set in monospace, which made a company name read
     like a code token. The `mono` class stays because tests/one-operator.test.mjs finds the byline by
     it; this rule is what the reader sees. */
  .foot__brand .mono {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .foot__tag {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 1rem 0 0.4rem;
    max-width: 32ch;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .foot__col h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faint);
    margin: 0 0 0.95rem;
  }

  .foot__col ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .foot__col a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding-block: 0.15rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .foot__col a:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .foot__base {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.6rem 1.5rem;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .foot__base p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .foot__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .foot__brand {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 460px) {
    .foot__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
